<title>NETHERLANDS: Road Air top Dutch IATA 96 aircargo revenue earner.</title>
<headline>Road Air top Dutch IATA 96 aircargo revenue earner.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Road Air Express headed the International Air Transport Association (IATA) sales revenue 'top 10' league of revenue-earning Dutch air cargo agents for 1996.</p>
<p>During the year, IATA said it recorded a 17.5 percent share of the Dutch market and a sales revenue of 179 million guilders.</p>
<p>Top 10 IATA forwarders in the Netherlands by sales revenue in 1996 in million guilders (with 1995 positions in parenthesis, followed by market share percentage)</p>
<p>					   Turnover 96  Turnover 95</p>
<p>1   (1)  Road Air	    17.5    179,014     168,141</p>
<p>2   (3)  Copex Air	    8.5     86,467     109,591</p>
<p>3   (5)  Air Express Intl   8.1     82,601	63,098</p>
<p>4   (2)  ChartAir	     6.5     66,204     113,211</p>
<p>5   (4)  Kuehne &amp; Nagel     4.5     46,191	74,629</p>
<p>6  (13)  Muller Air Freight 3.0     30,807	33,512</p>
<p>7  (16)  Visbeen		2.7     27,404	30,424</p>
<p>8  (22)  KDS Air		2.4     24,049	22,590</p>
<p>9   (7)  Nippon Express     2.1     21,483	45,807</p>
<p>10  (6)  MSAS		   2.1     21,417	55,950</p>
<p>Total turnover of the IATA agents in the Netherlands for 1996 was 1,02 billion guilders - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
